  "summary" : "Shell access was denied, so the notes below are derived from the Q/A pair itself (the answer states its claims were code-verified); independent re-verification is listed under open threads.\n\n```\nKNOWLEDGE NOTES — workflow-log.html: run waterfall + session follow-ups (openloop)\n==================================================================================\n\nSUBJECT\nworkflow-log.html (with workflow-log.js) shows how a workflow instance ran: all\npersonas incl. inner (nested) workflows and their parent relations, and lets the\nuser follow up on the finished run with ad-hoc prompts/questions. Follow-ups are\nexecuted as \"RUN items\" on the bottom-most persona of the session — the same RUN\nengine/grammar as graph.html's node RUNs, only anchored differently.\n\nDATA SOURCE\n- Fetch: /api/instances/:id/logs/sessions/:session -> LogHandler.getSessionLogs.\n- Payload = full waterfall of ONE run: `levels` + `logs`.\n- Each log row: personaId?, level, agent, msg.parents, input, output, success,\n  startedAt (used for tip selection).\n\nWATERFALL RENDERING\n- Rows with personaId != null -> node cards. Rows with personaId: null are\n  workflow scaffolding — BOTH the outer workflow frame AND inner-workflow\n  frames are filtered out; personas of inner workflows are kept, so nested\n  workflows' people are drawn (checkInnerPersonaFilter pins this).\n- Relations: drawEdges() draws one bezier per msg.parents entry; edges cross\n  inner-workflow boundaries whenever both endpoints are rendered cards.\n- Layout: one column per level (placeNodes / levelColumn). Extras: mini-map\n  grouped by level; duration-based speed tiers green/blue/red; per-persona\n  detail panel with CONTEXT / INPUT / RESULT bubbles.\n\nFOLLOW-UP PANEL (right panel, second and exclusive mode)\n- openFollowUpPanel. Auto-opens once on load iff sessionSuccess true; reopen\n  via \"Follow-up\" button under the mini-map.\n- Gating \"workflow finished\": frontend requires EVERY session log row success;\n  backend enforces same via sessionRunEnd() — a successful `run_ends` row is\n  the source of truth.\n- Footer state machine (same grammar as graph.html):\n  empty -> \"Seed original answer\" (POST .../seed) -> run in progress /\n  summarizing -> failed -> Retry -> success w/o summary -> \"write a summary\"\n  hint -> success + summary -> composer.\n- Seed (run 0) materializes the original answer: prompt = session's original\n  ask, output = tip persona's output; then a summarization pass. Empty summary\n  lands as `failed`, never `answered`.\n- Turns: POST .../graph/sessions/:sid/run with { prompt, parent_run_id: tip.id }.\n  Per-turn delete, failed-tip retry, manual summary edit\n  (PUT /graph/:nid/runs/:rid with the session UUID as :nid) — all reuse the\n  node-RUN contracts unchanged.\n\nRUN TARGET — sessionTip()\n- Target = persona log with max (level, startedAt): either the synthesized\n  `_bottom_` completion or the single persona of the last level.\n- Every follow-up re-executes THAT persona, with full fidelity\n  (sessionTipContext):\n  * Agent re-resolved from the recorded agent name via resolveSessionScript:\n    strip `openloop_` prefix; search project bin first, then user-local bin;\n    base scripts and unknown agents -> HTTP 400.\n  * Context files written into the run dir, referenced as `@`-prefixed lines\n    in the exec prompt:\n      ctx.md        = persona knowledge + MCPs collected across the\n                      instance->home chain\n      convo.md      = thread summaries up to the parent\n      parent-<id>.md = one per parent, containing its full output\n  * Arg shape mirrors the runner's tip-persona invocation: real personas get\n    [root, knowledgePath, prompt, about]; synthesized _bottom_ gets the\n    node-RUN 3-arg shape.\n\nSTORAGE & LIFECYCLE\n- Turns live in graph_run_logs anchored on the SESSION UUID; node_id is the\n  overloaded anchor column. `session_run` notification kind = marker row\n  written at insert time.\n- Lifecycle identical to node RUNs: progress -> summarizing -> success |\n  failed; tip-only appends; failed-tip retry; splice-on-delete with\n  reparenting.\n\nNET DIFFERENCE vs graph.html node RUNs (only two)\n1. Anchor: session UUID instead of node id.\n2. Executor is persona-faithful (knowledge path + system prompt + parents'\n   outputs) vs bare 3-arg node shape.\nDocumented in llms.txt under \"Graph sessions\".\n\nSETTLED DESIGN CHOICE WORTH KNOWING (with its trade-off)\n- Overloading graph_run_logs.node_id to hold the session UUID (plus a\n  session_run marker row) vs a dedicated sessions/sessions-runs table.\n  Chosen: overload. Trade-off: + full reuse of node-RUN contracts, queries,\n  and lifecycle code; - semantic overloading of node_id, so any consumer of\n  graph_run_logs must be aware session UUIDs can appear as node_id.\n\nOPEN THREADS\n- Not re-verified here: shell access denied; all names/paths above come from\n  the answer, which itself claims code-level confirmation. Cheap re-check:\n  grep for sessionTip, resolveSessionScript, sessionRunEnd,\n  checkInnerPersonaFilter, openFollowUpPanel, sessionTipContext; and read the\n  \"Graph sessions\" section of llms.txt.\n- Unverified specifics: exact thresholds for the green/blue/red speed tiers;\n  whether sessionSuccess gating checks every row's success flag or only the\n  final row (answer implies every row + backend run_ends); UI handling of the\n  400 on unknown/base agents during follow-up.\n- Worth pursuing: (a) do follow-up turns appear in the workflow-log waterfall\n  or only in the thread panel? (b) how do session_run marker rows affect other\n  graph_run_logs consumers (e.g., node run lists) — any filtering needed?\n  (c) collision risk between session UUIDs and real node ids in node_id, and\n  the migration path if sessions ever get their own table; (d) can a follow-up\n  turn itself trigger a nested workflow, and if so how sessionTip behaves on\n  the next turn.\n```",
  "prompt" : "`workflow-log.html` reveals how workflow ran, personas and inner workflows and their relations.\n\nFurthermore it allows a user to follow-up on a workflow and add ad-hoc changes or ask questions.\n\nEach follow-up is executed as \"RUN item\" on the bottom-most persona in a workflow, similar how \"RUN items\" are executed for nodes on `graph.html`.",
